{
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "autoloader-generic",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "The app ships no composer/autoload.php, so the server registers its generic loader for lib/ and looks every class up in the file system.",
        "  A composer/composer.json with config.vendor-dir \".\", config.optimize-autoloader true, a config.autoloader-suffix and autoload.psr-4 {\"OCA\\\\DropAccount\\\\\": \"../lib/\"} makes composer dump-autoload write composer/autoload.php with a class map; the code of the app does not change."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "job-time-sensitivity",
      "level": "info",
      "places": [
        "lib/BackgroundJob/TimedDeleteAccountData.php OCA\\DropAccount\\BackgroundJob\\TimedDeleteAccountData"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "1 timed job does not say whether it is time sensitive. A job that sets TIME_INSENSITIVE with setTimeSensitivity() is moved to the maintenance window of the server; whether a job is heavy enough for that only its maintainer knows.",
        "  lib/BackgroundJob/TimedDeleteAccountData.php OCA\\DropAccount\\BackgroundJob\\TimedDeleteAccountData"
      ]
    },
